## Conventions

- **Memory contract.** Every memory is one file with the frontmatter in [context/MEMORY-CONTRACT.md](context/MEMORY-CONTRACT.md), tagged from [context/topics.md](context/topics.md). Read it before writing memory.
- **Generated indexes.** Every `MEMORY.md`, `context/TOPICS-INDEX.md`, and `DIGEST.md` is built from `description` fields, so never hand-edit below a generated marker. Change the description and run `python agent-cooperation/memory-librarian/build_indexes.py` (`--adopt projects/<slug>` adds a project).
- **File naming.** Project memory goes in `projects/<slug>/` (kebab-case, check for an existing folder first) with a type prefix: `project_`, `feedback_`, `reference_`, `domain_`, or `lesson_`. Cross-project memory goes in `context/feedback/` or `context/reference/` without a prefix.
- **Wikilinks.** Link with `[[name]]`, resolved by frontmatter `name` (default: the filename stem, underscores to hyphens), so moves don't break links.
> **New here? Read [MAP.md](MAP.md) first.** It names the files to read at
> the start of a session and routes you to a project.

