- [Export-tool date corruption via %.6g](context/reference/export-sigfig-date-corruption.md) â€” Dates that are exact or exactly ONE DAY EARLY, never late, with no month or weekday pattern and a 25-day period: that is a Unix timestamp passed through
- [An external oracle validates the count, not the population](context/reference/external-oracle-validates-count-not-population.md) â€” A second source computed over the *same base tables* proves your arithmetic, not that you counted the right rows.
- [Git Push All / Pull All shortcuts](context/reference/git-sync-all-shortcuts.md) â€” Read before changing or debugging the Git Push All / Git Pull All desktop shortcuts on Swimba (built 2026-08-03), which commit+push or fast-forward every repo
- [Swimba headless access](context/reference/swimba-headless-access.md) â€” Read before touching remote access or the firewall on Swimba, the Ubuntu box with no monitor.
- [Workflow agents hit the response limit when the doc IS the return value](context/reference/workflow-agent-response-limit-truncation.md) â€” When a Workflow agent's return value IS a large document it hits the per-response token limit, and the harness keeps only the agent's LAST message - so the doc
- [Caleb's database access level](context/reference/caleb-db-access-level.md) â€” Caleb has READ-ONLY access to RRL's production databases - only two full-time devs in the org can write - yet he works on database projects constantly.
- [Python write_text() is cp1252 on Windows](context/reference/python-write-text-cp1252-windows.md) â€” `pathlib` read_text() / write_text() with no `encoding=` use the locale codec (cp1252) on Windows, so a directly-typed em-dash lands as a raw 0x97 and the UTF-8
- [Rscript: bare stdin() is the script source](context/reference/rscript-stdin-is-script-source.md) â€” Under `Rscript`, bare `stdin()` is the SCRIPT SOURCE, not the process's standard input: an interactive `readLines(n = 1L)` prompt silently returns a line of the
- [Assert the shape of a grouping](context/reference/assert-the-shape-of-groupings.md) â€” A bad grouping or join key does not raise, it collapses: `str(nan or "")` == "nan" fused a whole population into one component and silently emptied a candidate
- [Mutation-test your assertions](context/reference/mutation-test-your-assertions.md) â€” A test asserting "field X is load-bearing" is often tautological: delete X from the source and confirm the test actually fails.
- [RRL Customer Profile deck style](context/reference/rrl-customer-profile-deck-style.md) â€” The audited visual system behind RRL_Customer_Profile_MVP.pptx: navy bookends, white evidence slides, Georgia / Calibri typography, warm cards, the chart
- [PowerPoint deck workflow (RRL template + COM render)](context/reference/pptx-deck-workflow.md) â€” Read before building a branded PowerPoint deck from the RRL template.
- [Work desktop gdrive appfolder trap](context/reference/work-desktop-gdrive-appfolder-trap.md) â€” On the WORK desktop the rclone `gdrive` remote was mis-scoped to drive.appfolder, so pushes landed in Google Drive's HIDDEN app folder, invisible in the web UI.
