- [rclone dataset sync](project_rclone_sync.md) â€” rclone sync of gitignored dataset folders wired into the In / Out Button Sign in / Sign out flows. Implemented and working end to end 2026-05-30. The live backend is the work OneDrive since 2026-09-12, after IT consented to rclone's app; the remote is one settings string, which is why the switch cost one field.
- [Live rclone config - OneDrive backend](reference_rclone_live_config.md) â€” The live rclone setup for the In / Out Button dataset sync as of 2026-09-12: remote `onedrive` (work business drive) rooted at `data sync/projects`, 600 s timeout. Migrated from `gdrive:rock_river/projects` - 280 files, 1.699 GiB, zero differences. Each machine needs its own `rclone config` sign-in; the Google Drive steps here are historical.
- [In / Out Button app (core)](project_app_core.md) â€” The base In / Out Button applet: a .NET 8 WinForms app that runs `git pull` on sign-in and stage/commit/push on sign-out across every git repo discovered under user-selected folders. Holds the goal and implementation log; search roots in %APPDATA%\InOutButton\settings.json, commit message `MM-dd-yy updates`.
- [Sync direction defaults](feedback_rclone_direction.md) â€” Read before touching the rclone integration in In / Out Button. Always `rclone copy`, never `sync` or `bisync` (sync deletes); sign-out pushes data before git push, sign-in pulls after git pull; a per-repo rclone failure logs and continues instead of aborting the batch.
- [.rclone-sync.json config](reference_rclone_sync_config.md) â€” Read before adding a repo to the In / Out Button dataset sync. Schema and conventions for the `.rclone-sync.json` file each repo commits at its root to declare which gitignored folders sync and where they land on the remote.
