description: Standing rule, every session, no invitation needed - grow the model benchmark set passively. When a session meets a problem a cheap model would miss (a number that is only wrong once rebuilt from its inputs, right arithmetic over the wrong rows, a seam between two systems, a call that succeeds and does nothing, a test that checks less than it claims, an evaluation that diverges from the deployed rule, a second root cause under a fixed symptom, an environment limit invisible in code, a claim that outruns its evidence, anything that slipped past Fable or Astra and cost a loop), write a candidate stub to agent-cooperation/calibration-specimens/_candidates/<date>-<slug>.md BEFORE applying the fix, because the pre-fix commit is the specimen. Five minutes, one file. Invoke /specimen-capture for the three-question test, the stub template, the held-out rule, and promotion (promote_candidate.py scaffolds, an agent finishes the cards, Caleb rules on disagreements).
